{'symbol': 'ALXN', 'date': '2019-10-19 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Alexion Pharmaceuticals, Inc. Appoints Tanisha Carino as Executive Vice President and Chief Corporate Affairs Officer, with Effect from November 4, 2019', 'text': "Alexion Pharmaceuticals reported the appointment of Tanisha Carino, Ph.D., as Executive Vice President and the company's first Chief Corporate Affairs Officer. Dr. Carino will join Alexion on November 4, and will serve on the company's Executive Committee. In her role, Dr. Carino will oversee the creation of a newly integrated Corporate Affairs function that encompasses Alexion's corporate affairs activities, including high-level relations with domestic and international governments and global communications. Dr. Carino has been at the forefront of collaborative efforts to promote policies, research, and business practices supporting the fight against disease and improving the lives of patients. Prior to joining Alexion, Dr. Carino served as the Executive Director of FasterCures, a Center of the Milken Institute, whose mission is to put patients in the center of the healthcare system, break down unnecessary barriers to innovation, and accelerate biomedical research."}{'symbol': 'COST', 'date': '2019-10-19 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Costco Wholesale Sets Quarterly Cash Dividend Of $0.65 Per Share', 'text': 'SETS QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND OF $0.65PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'D', 'date': '2019-10-19 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Northam and Dominion Reach Deal to Power State Buildings with Renewable Energy', 'text': 'Gov. Ralph Northam and Dominion Energy announced that under a partnership, Dominion will provide the Commonwealth with 420 megawatts of renewable energy. The projects are: Rocky Forge Wind, under development by Apex Clean Energy in Botetourt County near Roanoke. It will be the first onshore wind project in Virginia. Belcher Solar, owned by Dominion Energy, in Louisa County, which was developed by a joint venture among Virginia Solar LLC and MAP Energy LLC. It will provide 88 megawatts at peak output. Bedford Solar in the City of Chesapeake is under development by Lincoln Clean Energy. It will provide 70 megawatts at peak output. Walnut Solar in King and Queen County is under development by Open Road Renewables. It will provide at least 90 megawatts at peak output. A fourth solar project will be named at a later time and will provide the remaining generation.'}{'symbol': 'DTE', 'date': '2019-10-19 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'DTE Midstream, A Non-Utility Business Of DTE Energy, Expands Growth Platform With Acquisition Of High-Quality Midstream Assets', 'text': "DTE MIDSTREAM, A NON-UTILITY BUSINESS OF DTE ENERGY, EXPANDS GROWTH PLATFORM WITH ACQUISITION OF HIGH-QUALITY MIDSTREAM ASSETS.DTE ENERGY CO - DEAL FOR $2.25 BILLION IN CASH.DTE ENERGY CO - WILL ACQUIRE 100 PERCENT OF ASSETS FROM MOMENTUM MIDSTREAM AND INDIGO NATURAL RESOURCES.DTE ENERGY CO - TO ALSO PAY $400 MILLION MILESTONE PAYMENT UPON COMPLETION OF GATHERING PIPELINE IN H2 2020.DTE ENERGY CO - ENTERED INTO AN AGREEMENT TO ACQUIRE A GATHERING SYSTEM AND GATHERING PIPELINE IN HAYNESVILLE SHALE FORMATION OF LOUISIANA.DTE ENERGY CO - TRANSACTION, AT A PROJECT LEVEL, IS IMMEDIATELY $0.15 ACCRETIVE TO OPERATING EPS IN 2020.DTE ENERGY CO - DTE REAFFIRMS COMMITMENT TO LONG-TERM BUSINESS MIX OF 70-75% UTILITY.DTE ENERGY CO - TRANSACTION HAS BEEN APPROVED BY DTE ENERGY'S BOARD OF DIRECTORS."}{'symbol': 'DXC', 'date': '2019-10-19 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'DXC Technology Appoints Mary E. Finch as Executive Vice President and Chief Human Resources Officer', 'text': "DXC Technology reported it has appointed Mary E. Finch as executive vice president and chief human resources officer (CHRO), reporting to company president and CEO Mike Salvino. Finch is the first senior leader hired since Salvino was named to his role in mid-September. Finch will lead all aspects of DXC Human Resources and employee engagement globally. Her responsibilities will include talent development and training; employee retention and recruitment; policy, benefits and compensation; workforce development and organization effectiveness; staffing and training; and global inclusion and diversity. She also becomes a member of DXC's senior leadership team. Finch joins DXC from AECOM, where she served as CHRO since 2015, with responsibility for all aspects of the company's global human resources organization. As a member of AECOM's executive team, she transformed the company's human resources practice by implementing a global talent strategy and new performance and productivity tools - while advancing employee training and development, career growth and workforce engagement initiatives."}{'symbol': 'INFO', 'date': '2019-10-19 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'IHS Markit - On Oct. 17 Board Approved Initiation Of Quarterly Cash Dividend Beginning In Q1 Of Fiscal 2020', 'text': 'IHS MARKIT LTD - ON OCTOBER 17 BOARD APPROVED INITIATION OF A QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND BEGINNING IN Q1 OF FISCAL 2020.IHS MARKIT LTD - ALSO AUTHORIZED A NEW SHARE REPURCHASE PROGRAM OF UP TO $2.5 BILLION OF IHS MARKIT COMMON SHARES.IHS MARKIT - SHARE REPURCHASE PROGRAM MAY BE FUNDED WITH EXISTING CASH, CASH EQUIVALENTS, MARKETABLE SECURITIES & FUTURE CASH FLOWS, OR THROUGH DEBT.'}{'symbol': 'K', 'date': '2019-10-19 16:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Kellogg Declares Regular Dividend Of $0.57 Per Share', 'text': 'KELLOGG COMPANY DECLARES REGULAR DIVIDEND OF $0.57 PER SHARE.SETS REGULAR DIVIDEND OF $0.57PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'MAR', 'date': '2019-10-19 04:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Marriott International To Acquire Elegant Hotels Group Fueling Growth Of All-Inclusive Platform', 'text': "MARRIOT INTERNATIONAL TO ACQUIRE ELEGANT HOTELS GROUP FUELING GROWTH OF ALL-INCLUSIVE PLATFORM.OFFER VALUES ENTIRE ISSUED AND TO BE ISSUED ORDINARY SHARE CAPITAL OF ELEGANT AT APPROXIMATELY £100.8 MILLION.UNDER TERMS OF OFFER, EACH ELEGANT SHAREHOLDER WOULD BE ENTITLED TO RECEIVE 110 PENCE PER ELEGANT SHARE.UPON COMPLETION OF PROPERTY RENOVATIONS, CO TO OPERATE ELEGANT HOTELS AS ALL-INCLUSIVE RESORTS UNDER ONE OR MORE OF MARRIOTT'S COLLECTION BRANDS."}{'symbol': 'ORCL', 'date': '2019-10-19 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Oracle says Mark Hurd Died On October 18, 2019', 'text': 'ORACLE CORP - MARK HURD, CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER AND DIRECTOR, DIED ON OCTOBER 18, 2019 - SEC FILING.'}{'symbol': 'CRM', 'date': '2019-10-19 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'salesforce.com, inc. Presents at 37th TBLI CONFERENCE ASIA, Nov-11-2019 02:00 PM', 'text': 'salesforce.com, inc. Presents at 37th TBLI CONFERENCE ASIA, Nov-11-2019 02:00 PM. Venue: The University of Chicago Francis and Rose Yuen Campus, 168 Victoria Rd, Mount Davis, Hong Kong Island, Hong Kong. Speakers: Samira Khan, Global Impact Manager.'}{'symbol': 'SYF', 'date': '2019-10-19 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Synchrony Financial Reports Third Quarter Net Earnings Of $1.1 Billion Or $1.60 Per Diluted Share', 'text': 'REPORTS THIRD QUARTER NET EARNINGS OF $1.1 BILLION OR $1.60 PER DILUTED SHARE.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.60.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.13 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY NET INTEREST INCOME INCREASED 4% TO $4.4 BILLION.Q3 2019 NET EARNINGS INCLUDES A $326 MILLION PRE-TAX, $248 MILLION AFTER-TAX, OR $0.38 PER DILUTED SHARE BENEFIT.BENEFIT FOR Q3 NET EARNINGS COMES FROM A REDUCTION IN RESERVE RELATED TO SALE OF WALMART CONSUMER PORTFOLIO.QTRLY PROVISION FOR LOAN LOSSES DECREASED $432 MILLION, OR 30%, TO $1.0 BILLION.QTRLY PURCHASE VOLUME GREW 5% TO $38.4 BILLION.'}{'symbol': 'VZ', 'date': '2019-10-19 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Verizon 5G Service Launches in Select Sports Arenas', 'text': 'After launching 5G service in several NFL stadiums last month, Verizon is now treating fans of other sports to its 5G coverage. Verizon is expanding its 5G coverage to select major sports arenas for the start of the NBA and NHL seasons. Here are the new arenas where Verizon customers can find 5G service: The carrier also promises that 5G will launch "soon" at Madison Square Garden in New York City, NY. Verizon plans to launch 5G coverage in 10 arenas during the 2019-2020 season.'}{'symbol': 'VRTX', 'date': '2019-10-19 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Vertex Announces Reimbursement of Cystic Fibrosis Medicines Symdeko® for Eligible Patients Ages 12 and Older, and Orkambi® in Children Ages 2 to 5, with Certain CFTR Mutations in Australia', 'text': 'Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated announced that SYMDEKO® (tezacaftor/ivacaftor and ivacaftor) is reimbursed in Australia for people with cystic fibrosis (CF) ages 12 years and older who are homozygous for the F508del mutation or who have one copy of the F508del mutation and another responsive residual function (RF) mutation in the cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator (CFTR) gene. People with CF who have one copy of the F508del mutation and another responsive RF mutation in the CFTR gene will have access to a medicine for the cause of their CF for the first time. In addition, ORKAMBI® (lumacaftor/ivacaftor) is now also reimbursed for the treatment of children with CF ages 2 to 5 who have two copies of the F508del mutation in the CFTR gene. Patients over the age of 6 have already been able to access ORKAMBI® in Australia since October 2018. Following previously received positive recommendations from the Pharmaceutical Benefits Advisory Committee (PBAC), eligible patients in Australia will be able to access both medicines immediately, and the medicines will be listed on the Pharmaceutical Benefits Scheme (PBS) from December 1st. Vertex’s CF medicines are reimbursed in 17 countries around the world including Austria, Denmark, Germany, the Republic of Ireland, Italy, the Netherlands, Sweden and the U.S.'}